Answer

"Currently, the number of requests depends on the AI provider's Rate Limits (RPM and TPM) and our server capacity. Gemini itself has limits on Requests Per Minute (RPM) and Tokens Per Minute (TPM), so if many users send requests simultaneously, we cannot simply forward every request directly to Gemini."

"In production, we should protect the AI service before the request reaches Gemini."

Interviewer: "How would you implement rate limiting?"
Answer

"I would implement rate limiting at multiple layers."

