The Most Important Part (Token Saving)

This is probably what the interviewer wants.

You can say:

"Yes. We stop the request before sending it to Gemini. Once the request reaches Gemini, even if Gemini rejects it or the request eventually fails, it may still count toward API rate limits or consume quota depending on the provider. Therefore, we perform authentication, validation, and rate limiting before making any AI API call. This prevents unnecessary API calls, saves cost, and avoids consuming available RPM."

